# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/003_bundled_header_inclusion.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_bundled_header_inclusion
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Inclusion of the compiler's own bundled freestanding headers, each exercised by a value or a relation it defines rather than merely by being named: stddef, stdint, stdarg, stdbool, limits, float, stdalign, stdnoreturn and iso646
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
HEADER EXCEPTION AND ITS REASON. This program takes the second of the corpus's two
sanctioned header exceptions and is the only program that takes it: see
tests/conformance/README.md, section "The two sanctioned header exceptions", under the
bolded paragraph beginning "Exception 2". It may include the nine REQUIRED bundled
freestanding headers -- stddef.h, stdint.h, stdarg.h, stdbool.h, limits.h, float.h,
stdalign.h, stdnoreturn.h and iso646.h -- and nothing else. Reason: it is the only place
the suite exercises include/ at all, and restricting it to <stdarg.h> as area 07 is
restricted would leave eight of the nine shipped headers included by nothing, which is a
coverage hole rather than a discipline. All nine are documented as shipped
(docs/technical-specifications.md line 19, with the per-header contents tabulated at
lines 202-214), and all nine are also freestanding headers the reference compiler
provides, which is what keeps the program compilable under both sides of oracle (a). No
header outside the nine is included; in particular stdio.h is not included, because bcc
ships none, so including it would succeed on the reference side and fail on the side
under test -- a divergence manufactured by the test rather than found in the compiler,
which is strictly worse than having no test at all. printf is therefore still
hand-declared, exactly as in every other corpus program. The bonus stdatomic.h is
deliberately excluded as well, even though the compiler ships it: it is not among the nine
required headers, no requirement mandates it, and atomics can require -latomic, which is
not in the shared flag set, so an inclusion would risk a link failure attributable to the
test.

Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- No signed integer overflow. Every printed value is a small int, a fixed-width limit
  cast to int, or a 0/1 relation.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- The only division-like operator is the unsigned remainder in two of the alignment
  relations. Its divisor is the non-zero constant 8 and both operands are unsigned, so
  neither a division by zero nor a sign conversion can arise.
- NO POINTER-TO-INTEGER CONVERSION of any kind, and the only pointer arithmetic is the
  arithmetic the language performs for a subscript: aligned_buf is subscripted at the
  literal indices 0 and 15 of a sixteen-element array, so every access stays inside the
  object. The null pointer is only ever compared, never printed or converted, and no
  pointer value is printed at all.
- No aliasing violation. The only object written after its declaration is the static
  alignas-qualified array aligned_buf, whose two unsigned char stores are separate
  statements and are read back in a later statement, never in the expression that wrote
  them.
- No read of uninitialized storage. The static object has static storage duration and is
  therefore zero-initialized before either store; both bytes that are printed are stored
  first.
- The variadic helper is exercised end to end and correctly: va_copy is taken before the
  original list has been read, so both lists start at the same position; each list is
  created or copied exactly once and ended exactly once in the same function; the second
  traversal reads the copy, never the exhausted original; and neither list is read past
  the number of arguments actually supplied.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points, and nothing depends on
  unspecified evaluation order: every call passes at most one side-effecting argument.
- printf is hand-declared with a prototype matching its use, and every format specifier
  matches the promoted type of its argument: every %d receives an int, after an explicit
  cast wherever the source was size_t, a comparison result or a fixed-width type.
- offsetof is applied only to a struct with int8_t and int32_t members, never one
  containing int64_t, because the i386 System V ABI aligns int64_t to 4 inside a struct
  while the other three targets align it to 8, so the offsets are 4 and 8 on every
  target and can be asserted exactly.
- Determinism: no address and no pointer value is printed or converted; no plain-char
  signedness-dependent value and no raw width-dependent value is printed; no long double
  appears; no translation-date, translation-time or source-name macro is consulted; and
  there is no randomness and no locale-dependent formatting. Output is a fixed 21-line
  sequence, one line per header property claimed, so a single divergent line localizes
  the defect to one header fact.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing
  is opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is
  read, and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires, so no exit status is
  truncated by the operating system.
- No deviation from the default warning gate is requested, and none is needed. The
  seven-flag gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
  produces zero diagnostics in the single native compile-only invocation the suite makes
  of it, and the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all
  compiles clean in its one instrumented native build, then runs to completion with empty
  stderr and exit status 0 and prints the golden stdout byte for byte.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
WIDTH NORMALIZATION is the central constraint on this program, and it is what lets all
four targets stay directly comparable with no target restriction, no disabled oracle and
no divergence marker. Per the authoritative target table at
docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462, x86_64-linux-gnu has pointer 8 and long 8
(ELF64), i686-linux-gnu has pointer 4 and long 4 (ELF32), and aarch64-linux-gnu and
riscv64-linux-gnu have pointer 8 and long 8 (ELF64). size_t, ptrdiff_t and intptr_t follow
the pointer, so each is 4 bytes on i686 and 8 bytes on the other three -- measured on this
branch as 4, 4, 4 on i686 against 8, 8, 8 on each of the others. Every fact that depends
on one of those widths is therefore printed ONLY as a 0/1 relation -- size_t_eq_ptr,
ptrdiff_eq_ptr, intptr_eq_ptr -- or as an inequality with margin -- int_max_ge_32767,
dbl_dig_ge_10. Each relation is 1 on all four targets precisely BECAUSE the widths move
together, so the line still carries a real claim about the headers while staying
byte-identical everywhere.

NO RAW WIDTH-DEPENDENT VALUE IS PRINTED ANYWHERE, and the exclusion is drawn by name
rather than left to intention. sizeof(void *), sizeof(size_t), sizeof(ptrdiff_t) and
sizeof(intptr_t) appear only inside the three relations above, where each is consumed by a
comparison and never reaches the output. sizeof(long), sizeof(max_align_t), LONG_MAX,
ULONG_MAX, SIZE_MAX, PTRDIFF_MAX, INTPTR_MAX, UINTPTR_MAX and every LDBL_ macro are absent
from the program entirely. The widest aligned type is the clearest case for why the rule is
drawn this widely: it was measured at 32 bytes on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64 and 48 bytes
on i686, so printing it would have manufactured a divergence that says nothing about the
compiler.

STRUCT MEMBER OFFSETS. The struct that offsetof is applied to carries only int8_t and
int32_t members. That is deliberate and measured: the i386 System V ABI aligns int64_t to
4 inside a struct while the other three targets align it to 8, so a struct containing an
int64_t yields a member offset of 4 on i686 against 8 on each of the other three, and would
turn a correct compiler into an apparent divergence.
With int32_t members the offsets are 4 and 8 on every target, so offsetof_b and offsetof_c
are asserted as exact values rather than hedged. alignof(int32_t) == 4 and
alignof(int8_t) == 1 likewise hold on all four targets, which is why those two are exact
values too.

ALIGNMENT IS OBSERVED THROUGH A LANGUAGE PROPERTY, NOT THROUGH AN ADDRESS, and this is the
one implementation-defined hazard the program had to be redesigned around. The corpus
rules permit an alignment residue and forbid printing an address; this program satisfies
that rule a fortiori, by performing no pointer-to-integer conversion at all. The alignas
specifier is applied to a struct MEMBER, so the requirement it imposes becomes a property
of a TYPE, and alignof reports that property directly: C11 6.7.5p2 makes 8 the member's
alignment requirement, a structure's requirement is at least that of each of its members,
and C11 6.2.8p1 makes every alignment a power of two, so alignof(struct AlignedHolder) >= 8
holds BY THE LANGUAGE rather than by any target ABI.

EVERY ONE OF THE THREE ALIGNMENT FACTS IS PRINTED AS A RELATION RATHER THAN AS AN EXACT
VALUE, and that is what the language actually guarantees: an implementation may align more
strictly than requested, and C11 6.7.2.1p15 lets it insert additional padding between
members, so alignof >= 8, an offset that is nonzero and divisible by 8, and a size
divisible by 8 are guaranteed while alignof == 8 and offsetof == 8 are not. The relations
still fail exactly when the request is ignored -- the member would then sit at offset 1,
which is neither divisible by 8 nor consistent with a structure alignment of 8 -- so
nothing is given up by declining to pin the padding this implementation happened to
choose.

THE ALIGNMENT CHECK OBSERVES NO ADDRESS RESIDUE, AND THE REASON IS THE STANDARD. Converting
the alignas-qualified object's address to uintptr_t and asserting that its residue modulo 8
is zero would not follow from equal width: C11 7.20.1.4p1 and 6.3.2.3p6 guarantee only that
a pointer converted to uintptr_t and back COMPARES EQUAL to the original, never that the
integer's low bits are the address's low bits. Whether a residue reflects alignment is a
property of the target ABI rather than of the header set this program tests, so no residue
is observed here, and the alignas-qualified OBJECT is exercised instead by a defined byte
round trip through an unsigned char lvalue, which reads and writes storage without observing
an address. Nothing is lost: alignas and alignof are both still
exercised, the qualified storage is still written and read back, and address-residue
observation is owned by 10_declarations_and_types/007_alignof_alignas.c, whose subject that
is and which carries the two-step pointer-carrier discipline the observation needs.

CHARACTER SIGNEDNESS. Plain char is never used for a printed value: signedness was
measured signed on x86_64 and i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64, so the character
limits are read through SCHAR_MIN and SCHAR_MAX and fixed-width values through int8_t,
each of which is -128 and 127 on all four targets.

long double IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Its representation was measured at 16, 12, 16 and 16
bytes across the four targets -- x87 80-bit against IEEE binary128 -- so naming it would
forfeit the byte-identical output this nine-header probe depends on. The type is not
dropped from the suite: it is written and run by
13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, whose own record excludes
cross-backend value equality alone and carries the marker XD-TYPE-LONGDOUBLE-001 scoped to
oracle (b) that the record format requires beside any narrowing. That division of labour is
why this record needs no marker of its own.

THE BONUS ATOMICS HEADER IS EXCLUDED, and the exclusion is recorded here as well as in
ub_notes because it is a narrowing of what this probe covers rather than an
undefined-behaviour argument: stdatomic.h is not among the nine required headers, no
requirement mandates it, and atomics can require -latomic, which is not in the shared flag
set -- so including it would risk a link failure attributable to the test rather than to
the compiler. The nine required headers are covered in full; the bonus header is the one
member of the shipped set this program does not reach, and that is the whole of the gap.

STANDARD-VERSION AND ARCHITECTURE PREDEFINED MACROS are not examined here; they are the
subject of 004_predefined_macros in this area, which asserts them only as relations.

NOTHING IS NARROWED. No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled, no warning-gate
deviation is requested and no marker is carried, so this block records the properties that
were normalized away rather than a coverage exclusion -- which is the point of recording
them: it makes the set of comparisons deliberately not made as visible as the set that
was. All twelve cells -- four targets by three optimization levels -- produce byte-identical
stdout and exit status 0, which is what lets oracle (b) compare the four backends without
narrowing and oracle (c) hold these bytes as the golden record.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
char_bit=8
schar_min=-128 schar_max=127
int8_min=-128 int8_max=127
uint16_max=65535
sizeof_int32=4 sizeof_int64=8
alignof_int32=4 alignof_int8=1
offsetof_b=4 offsetof_c=8
size_t_eq_ptr=1
ptrdiff_eq_ptr=1
intptr_eq_ptr=1
int_max_ge_32767=1
null_compares_equal=1
bool_true=1 bool_iso646_and=1
iso646_macros_present=1
flt_radix=2 dbl_dig_ge_10=1
alignas_type_alignment=1
alignas_member_offset=1
alignas_size_multiple=1
alignas_object_roundtrip=1
noreturn_macro_present=1
varargs_two_passes=120
END
